.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/raw/
data/chroma_bench/

# Never commit real secrets. .env.example is the tracked template and IS committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated by scripts/build_index.py. Reproducible from source.
# NOTE: data/chunking_report.json is deliberately NOT listed here. tests/test_faq.py
# reads it as a fixture, so a clone needs it present to run the suite.
#
# NOTE: data/chunks.jsonl and data/chroma/ are deliberately NOT ignored either, and that
# reverses part of the previous policy. A deployed copy of this app is built from this
# repo and has no shell, so the index has to arrive with the code: leaving it out made
# every hosted deploy open on "No index found. Build it first: python
# scripts/build_index.py", which is a command a hosted Streamlit app cannot run. The
# cost is ~3.2 MB (chunks.jsonl 133 KB + chroma/ 3.0 MB) for 168 chunks, and the win is
# a cold start that answers immediately. app.py still rebuilds the index itself if it is
# ever missing, so a fresh clone does not depend on the committed copy being current.
# Refresh them with: .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\build_index.py --refresh
data/clean/
data/documents.json
data/ingest_log.json

# Editors and OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
.pytest_cache/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
